{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnxsfsQyd8ycnLJyqg4MPN","type":"tool_result","content":"71:- 731 Tile map; E.TileMap: map\n733:- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], typ\n734:- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n737:- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n738:- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n739:- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n740:- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n747:- `map.drawFloor(r)`: draw the baked floor (first thing in draw, after r.sky); walls come from queueWalls(r)\n762:- `map.queueWalls(r)`: queue every visible wall box. Call once per frame after drawFloor.\n776:- `map.blocked`: cells nobody can walk on (deep water, lava, pits): legend { floor: 'water', block: true } or TileMap { block: ['water'] }\n835:- `E.tex`: floor textures for a TileMap's floorTex(x, y), each giving [r, g, b] at a world point; as materials too: floorMat: 'grass'\n836:- `E.tex.checker(x, y, o = {})`: checkerboard tiles (castle floors, bonus rooms). o: { a, b, size }\n837:- `E.tex.dirt(x, y, o = {})`: dirt, sand or snow: base color with soft noise and specks. o: { base, dark, light }\n838:- `E.tex.flagstone(x, y, pal, size = 16)`: stone flagstones with running-bond rows. pal: {stones:[hex..], mortar, hi, lo, speck}\n839:- `E.tex.grass(x, y, o = {})`: grass with darker tufts and a few flowers. o: { base, dark, light, flower } hex colors\n840:- `E.tex.plain(x, y, o = {})`: plain color with light noise, for roads, carpets and space floors. o: { base, amount }\n841:- `E.tex.planks(x, y, o = {})`: wooden floor boards running along x. o: { base, dark, line }\n842:- `E.tex.water(x, y, o = {})`: water with static ripple lines (baked, so it does not move). o: { base, dark, light }\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1202:- `game.gpu.map = null` †: the TileMap it measures walls on\n1433:- `fog.draw(r, T = 16, o = {})`: draw it over the world: unseen cells black, seen ones dimmed (o.dim: .55, o.color), walls' faces covered too; call after the world and before the HUD. T: world units a cell; o.height(cx, cy): a cell's top (a TileMap's heig\n1440:- `E.Grid.from(map, o = {})`: a grid from a TileMap: its walkable cells (o.tops: true stands on the walls' tops at their heights, for tactics)\n1487:- `E.tint(r, cells, color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height = null)`: tints on cells' tops: E.tint(r, cells ([[cx, cy], ...]), color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height(cx, cy) = 0): a move range, a path, an attack's reach, drawn on the floor (decals) where height is 0\n1496:- `mode7.drawFloor(g, vp)`: draw the floor below the horizon in the rectangle ({ x, y, w, h }), a row at a time, and the fog over it\n1710:- `strategy.map` †: the TileMap it stands on (a building blocks its cells)\n107:  play: { pausable: true, view: 'side', input: 'PLATFORMER', res: 'snes', views: ['side', 'brawler'], touch: ['jump', 'attack'],\n111:`game.go(name, data)` switches before the next step, through a short dithered fade (`game.fadeTime`; `{ fade: 0 }` cuts; `{ fade: 'wipe' | 'iris' | 'mosaic' | 'swirl' | 'dissolve' | 'white', seconds: .4, at: hero }` a transition, a plain fade under reduce motion); timers and particles are cleared. `pausable: true` lets Escape / P / Start pause it and opens the pause menu (below). `view`, `views`, `input`, `res`, `expand`, `touch`, `propSize` are applied on entry. A scene's `back()` takes a phone's back gesture first (return true when it went back somewhere: a sub-menu closed).\n130:With no code: a **pause menu** on pausable scenes (Resume, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title; keys, mouse, gamepad and touch), **settings** saved per game (`game.settings`: volume, music, effects, mute, reduce motion, screen shake and flashes, pixel scaling, a screen filter: clean, scanlines or CRT, the frame rate: Auto, 60 or Full, and its readout), **controls** the player rebinds (conflicts said first; dead zone, invert aim, button symbols, vibration; touch button side, size, opacity), **full screen** (a phone's first tap and each game started by a tap, a top-right button, the menu; turning it off is remembered), a **menu button** at the top right (on a touch screen it stays in play: it is the touch START), a **way out** of every menu screen (close, back, a sideways swipe), the **back gesture** stepping back in the game (`game.back()`: a menu screen closes, play pauses) before it leaves the page, **pausing** when the page is hidden or the controller unplugs, and a page set up for phones (safe areas, no scrolling, zooming or pull to refresh on the canvas).\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and q\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in an","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45b3a95a-0877-4e80-ba88-5e087b153b9c","uuid":"610100f6-abe2-4dc4-b67d-ac35ab47a6b4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:56:34.585Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"71:- 731 Tile map; E.TileMap: map\n733:- `new E.TileMap(o = {}) → map`: Walls standing on a floor (top-down, isometric, brawler). Either { rows: [...ASCII...], legend: { '#': 1, '@': 'hero' }, types, floorTex } (recommended) or { w, h, cells: [ids...], floor: [tags...], blocked: [0 | 1...], typ\n734:- `new E.TileMap({ types })`: types[id] = { h, top, side, line, course, cut, cutH, face, roof }\n735:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].face })`: the wall's material (E.MATERIALS): 'brick' (default) | 'stone' | 'rock' | 'plank' | 'timber' | 'plaster' | 'hedge' | 'none' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n736:- `new E.TileMap({ types[id].roof })`: the top's material: 'speckle' (default) | 'plain' | 'tiles' (roof shingles) | 'slab' (paving) | 'leaves' | 'grass' | any material id or '#hex pattern'\n737:- `new E.TileMap({ floorTex })`: floorTex(x, y, floorTag, view) -> [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, glow]\n738:- `new E.TileMap({ floorMat, floorMats })`: a material for the floor, floorMats: { tag: material } for tagged cells (in place of floorTex)\n739:- `new E.TileMap({ block })`: ['water', 'lava'] floor tags nobody can walk on (or put block: true in a legend entry)\n740:- `new E.TileMap({ chunks })`: bake the floor in squares near the camera (true, false; by default a map of more than 128 x 128 cells)\n747:- `map.drawFloor(r)`: draw the baked floor (fir